Notebook[{
Cell["Hypergraph", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"1ea26566-fe70-2747-9fb8-a2b53071e712"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypergraph", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"edge1", ",", " ", "edge2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f32710c5-143c-b542-9304-aebd21f401d0"],
 " ",
 "builds a hypergraph from a list of Edge objects; its vertex set is the \
union of the vertices of those edges."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"c2b9695a-2c2b-8144-baf8-b683a34ac887"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypergraph", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"v1", ",", " ", "v2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", "...", "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "...", "}"}], ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "bd513ef3-9f3b-4644-8161-74f4c4842897"],
 " ",
 "builds a hypergraph on an explicit vertex list, with edges given as lists \
of vertex identifiers, directed and unlabelled by default."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"d3d2fbb3-1d08-ad4a-9229-64889950dd06"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypergraph", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"v1", ",", " ", "v2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6120ea44-ebb1-5244-ba86-c7d972c6bc98"],
 " ",
 "builds an edgeless hypergraph on the given vertices."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"6f671270-cd5e-8c4e-852b-72560c7e9410"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"3e6fa4b4-3a8f-4146-8118-1be3e89d942b"],

Cell["\<\
A Hypergraph is a multiset of edges: the order of the edges carries no \
information, and a repeated edge counts once for each occurrence.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"cf4f7f7b-9072-bf4d-8db7-034c1f2546bf"],

Cell["\<\
The vertex list and the edge list are both put into a canonical order when \
the hypergraph is built, so two ways of writing the same hypergraph produce \
literally the same expression and may be compared with ===.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"00b0e29f-8550-8d46-b081-5664ef8e5811"],

Cell["\<\
Vertices occurring only inside edges are absorbed into the vertex set.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a5dfa2a9-06df-2040-ad7d-5bbdee130aaf"],

Cell["\<\
A label attached to any occurrence of a vertex propagates to every other \
occurrence of that identifier. If two occurrences disagree, the explicit \
vertex list wins and the message Hypergraph::vlbl is produced.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"24c81425-b5be-9044-9bf4-eb4c4b1121c2"],

Cell["\<\
A Hypergraph displays as a drawing of itself, the way a Graph does; see \
HypergraphPlot. Feeding the displayed output back to the kernel recovers the \
object. A hypergraph too large to draw usefully displays as a summary box \
instead; see HypergraphLargeQ.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ed0cf70e-a98a-1843-82be-efe72bcd7063"],

Cell["\<\
VertexList, EdgeList, VertexCount and EdgeCount work directly on a \
Hypergraph. They are protected System` symbols, extended here with UpValues \
rather than redefined.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"029851f9-928f-cd40-9bc1-937646239fc1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Properties are read as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"hg", "[", "\"\<prop\>\"", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"1553c436-d49a-7044-aba6-b434634d815a"],
 ". The available properties are given by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"hg", "[", "\"\<Properties\>\"", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"0cf2fde2-7a78-4243-8a91-82eb5f45ab80"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7bff23dd-4327-c642-85b9-a32e4fde1de3"],

Cell["\<\
An invalid specification produces the message Hypergraph::spec and returns \
$Failed.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"eb6b6661-dd36-264c-ade4-35cb440fc006"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"fecbae4f-4d75-a244-92f7-63e2b7a3e3de"],

Cell["From a list of edges; the vertex set is inferred:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"da182317-0f57-e444-a1d5-33050f8e4f71"],

